<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anushteginid dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anushteginid dynasty was the ruling house of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anushtegin-gharchai">Anushtegin Gharchai</a>. Initially governors for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>, its rulers gradually won independence and, under Tekish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-ad-din-muhammad-ii">Ala ad-Din Muhammad II</a>, built a large empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. The dynasty was destroyed by the Mongol invasion in the early thirteenth century.</p></div>
